ne\n--\nImplemented and pushed LALAL API v1 backend (commits 68ceb76, 28794f7). Includes v1 upload/split/check/limits/cancel/delete, durable source/task/idempotency checkpoints with fail-closed ambiguity handling, bounded polling and WAV download validation, effective-model pinning, mocked HTTP tests, and an opt-in manual smoke-test procedure. Verified: 55 backend/project tests and 19 analysis tests pass (3 pre-existing Python deprecation warnings).\n--\nauthor:\tmrkkucharski\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\tfalse\nstatus:\tnone\n--\nFix cycle 1 complete: source-upload reuse is now durable and scoped by content hash, so the four original-source operations share one LALAL upload while the instrumental cascade uploads separately. Task/idempotency state remains operation-local. Added regression coverage; ============================= test session starts ==============================\nplatform darwin -- Python 3.11.15, pytest-9.1.1, pluggy-1.6.0\nrootdir: /Users/marekkucharski/projects/.pm-worktrees/vgt/issue-45\nconfigfile: pyproject.toml\nplugins: anyio-4.14.2\ncollected 27 items\n\ntests/test_lalal.py .....                                                [ 18%]\ntests/test_separation.py ......................                          [100%]\n\n============================== 27 passed in 0.64s ============================== passes (27 tests). Pushed commit b8b5d08.\n--\nauthor:\tmrkkucharski\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\tfalse\nstatus:\tnone\n--\nFix cycle 2 complete: preflight now uploads and prices authoritative source durations before any split, persists/reuses that source identity, and reserves the cascade. Expired task recovery creates and checkpoints a new idempotency identity only when required local output recovery is needed; downloads now validate task-reported duration against WAV metadata. Verified with `uv run pytest -q tests/test_lalal.py tests/test_separation.py` (31 passed).\n--\nauthor:\tmrkkucharski\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\tfalse\nstatus:\tnone\n--\nFix cycle 3 complete: preflight now reuses any unexpired, durably checkpointed LALAL upload identity and persists a replacement source identity immediately if it has expired, so a credit check never causes a gratuitous re-upload. Added mocked-v1 regression coverage. Verified with `uv run pytest -q tests/test_lalal.py tests/test_separation.py` (32 passed).\n--\n6dea7cc (HEAD -> issue-48-m1-f-stem-separation-evaluation-pass-on) M1-B: LALAL API v1 backend (LalalSeparator) (#51)\n8360951 chore(pm): start review issue #45 (claude)\n7923e38 chore(pm): start issue #47 (codex)\n17d31f2 chore(pm): start issue #47 (codex)\n61c1049 chore(pm): start fix issue #45 (codex)\n66a7440 chore(pm): start review issue #45 (codex)\nfdd2c77 chore(pm): start fix issue #45 (codex)\na04098d chore(pm): start issue #46 (codex)\n0188ee5 chore(pm): start review issue #45 (codex)\n9956419 chore(pm): start fix issue #45 (codex)\n8ea4696 chore(pm): start review issue #45 (codex)\nb84ee65 chore(pm): start issue #45 (codex)\n3ca76c5 Merge pull request #50 from mrkkucharski/issue-44-m1-e-consolidate-vgt-artifacts-under-a-v\n36b5c80 chore(pm): start review issue #44 (codex)\nbac595f chore(pm): start issue #45 (codex)\n315e736 chore(pm): start issue #45 (codex)\n+ main\n  remotes/origin/HEAD -> origin/main\n  remotes/origin/main\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
